<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov soybean imports fall 8.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov soybean imports fall 8.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in November totalled 252,599 tonnes, 8.4 percent lower than the same month a year earlier, according to Finance Ministry data released on Thursday.</p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Nov 96     Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Total imports     252,599    515,877     275,752</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		  213,866    338,882     228,713</p>
<p> Bolivia		16,354     ----	   ----</p>
<p> Paraguay	     12,255     91,729	17,240</p>
<p>Imports in the first 11 months of 1996 totalled 4.4 million tonnes against 4.3 million tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (81-3-3432-7431)</p>
</text>
